---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Import a Postman Collection v2.0 or v2.1 export

Usage: rustman import postman [OPTIONS] <SRC>

Arguments:
  <SRC>
          The exported file (or folder, for Bruno and .http sources)

Options:
      --into <DIR>
          Collection folder to write into, inside the workspace (default: the slug of the source collection's name)

      --dry-run
          Convert and print the planned files and secrets without writing anything

      --on-conflict <POLICY>
          When a file already exists: keep it, replace it, or write next to it
          
          [default: skip]
          [possible values: skip, overwrite, rename]

      --report <FILE>
          Also write the report as JSON (rustman.import-report/v1) to FILE

      --migration-report <FILE>
          Write the unconverted script statements, with suggestions, as Markdown to FILE

      --max-size <SIZE>
          Refuse sources larger than this (bytes, or with K, M or G; default 100M)

      --fail-on-unsupported
          Exit with 1 when a feature was unsupported, dropped or unmapped

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
